# The build context, by allowlist.
#
# ``Dockerfile`` builds a wheel from four paths and nothing else, so everything
# is excluded first and those four are let back in. An allowlist rather than a
# list of exclusions because the failure modes point opposite ways: a forgotten
# exclusion silently ships a virtualenv, a private inventory or a .git history
# into the build context, while a forgotten inclusion fails the build loudly.
*

!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!LICENSE
!src

# Nothing under src/ that is not source: a stale __pycache__ from the host would
# be copied in and shadow the code it was compiled from if the interpreters ever
# disagreed, and .pyc files are rebuilt by pip anyway.
src/**/__pycache__
src/**/*.py[cod]
